        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r192578592-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "for a spiritual you",
        "text": "Considered to be one of the most important temples dedicated to Lord Shiva is a holy destination for Hindus. It also is one of the UNESCO world heritage sites. Located on the bank of river Bagmati in kathmandu in one of the busiest areas of the city, it is easily accessible by all sorts of public and private transportation system. Though the main temple permits only Hindus inside but the premises around are open to people from all the religions and the atmosphere is spiritual enough for everyone regardless of religion. The place might seem chaotic in the first look but there is a different kid of peace among the chaos, the nagas and the yogis sitting all around the temple, the old ladies sitting in groups and singing, the pigeons, monkeys and cows, the hustle- bustle is one of a kind. There are shops around selling prasad and stuffs like rudraksha and pearls but I would advise everyone to be careful while buying such stuffs ensuring that it's original stuff and don't hesitate to bargain. So, Pashupati has got something for everyone it's a place full of goodness and positive vibes and an experience one of it's kind !",
