        "text": "My wife and I were struggling with whether to visit or not, but we found the temple grounds to be well kept (better than many places in Kathmandu - and restoration is ongoing under the auspices of UNESCO) and the experience of seeing these cremation ghats does give one pause, but was very moving nonetheless. If you don't plan on going to Varanasi or other sacred Hindu sites, this is a manageable and interesting place to spend an hour. Also, close to the airport, so very convenient.",
